== Mock Examination 1 — Questions

#mcq(1, [Which of these would be a symptom of damage to the cerebellum?], [Loss of memory], [Loss of speech], [Loss of vision], [Loss of balance and coordination])

#mcq(2, [Colour blindness is caused by], [a defect in the rods], [damage to the iris], [a defect in the cones of the retina], [a clouded lens])

#mcq(3, [The hormone that increases the rate of metabolism is], [insulin], [thyroxine], [ADH], [adrenaline])

#mcq(4, [Insect-pollinated flowers usually have], [bright petals, scent and nectar], [no petals], [feathery stigmas outside the flower], [very small amounts of pollen])

#mcq(5, [Menstruation occurs when], [an egg is fertilised], [ovulation occurs], [the placenta forms], [the lining of the uterus breaks down because no embryo has implanted])

#mcq(6, [The adult insect that emerges from the final moult is called the], [nymph], [imago], [instar], [pupa])

#mcq(7, [Which of these would most reduce the spread of a droplet infection in a classroom?], [Closing the windows], [Sharing water bottles], [Opening the windows and covering the mouth when coughing], [Sitting closer together])

#mcq(8, [Yeast reproduces by], [budding], [binary fission], [spores only], [sexual reproduction only])

#mcq(9, [Which of these is a public-health measure against malaria?], [Boiling drinking water], [Vaccinating against tuberculosis], [Wearing shoes], [Using insecticide-treated nets])

#mcq(10, [If 20 snails are marked and a second sample of 20 contains 4 marked, the estimated population is], [80], [100], [120], [160])

#mcq(11, [A neurone is best described as], [a cell that contracts], [a gland], [a nerve cell that conducts impulses], [a blood vessel])

#mcq(12, [Long sight (hypermetropia) is corrected by], [a convex lens], [a concave lens], [a plain glass], [a prism])

#mcq(13, [A deficiency of ADH causes], [diabetes mellitus], [goitre], [cretinism], [diabetes insipidus — the production of large volumes of dilute urine])

#mcq(14, [The advantage of vegetative propagation in agriculture is that], [the desirable qualities of the parent are preserved], [the offspring vary widely], [it always produces stronger plants], [it produces seeds])

#mcq(15, [The structure that carries the egg from the ovary to the uterus is the], [cervix], [oviduct], [urethra], [vagina])

#mcq(16, [The main advantage of a pupal stage is that it], [allows the insect to feed heavily], [lets the insect fly], [provides a protected stage in which the body is rebuilt], [helps the insect to reproduce])

#mcq(17, [Typhoid fever is spread mainly by], [droplets in the air], [contaminated food and water], [mosquito bites], [direct skin contact])

#mcq(18, [Mould on bread is a], [fungus], [bacterium], [virus], [protozoan])

#mcq(19, [Tar in tobacco smoke], [helps the lungs to clear], [carries oxygen], [contains carcinogens and paralyses the cilia], [is harmless])

#mcq(20, [The dependent variable is the one that is], [changed by the experimenter], [kept constant], [estimated], [measured as a result])

#mcq(21, [Which of these is a function of the cerebrospinal fluid?], [It cushions the brain and spinal cord against shock], [It carries oxygen to the muscles], [It digests bacteria], [It stores memories])

#mcq(22, [The ear is also important for balance because of the], [cochlea], [semicircular canals], [pinna], [Eustachian tube])

#mcq(23, [Insulin is secreted by the], [liver], [adrenal medulla], [islets of Langerhans in the pancreas], [thyroid])

#mcq(24, [The part of the flower that protects the bud before it opens is the], [petal], [anther], [stigma], [sepal])

#mcq(25, [Menopause is best described as], [the beginning of menstruation], [a disease of the uterus], [the permanent end of the menstrual cycle], [the loss of the uterus])

#mcq(26, [Mosquito control by removing stagnant water works because], [the adult cannot fly without water], [the eggs die in dry air only in winter], [the adult lays eggs only in clean water], [the larva and pupa are aquatic and cannot move to another pool])

#mcq(27, [A pathogen is best defined as], [an organism that causes disease], [any organism that carries a disease], [a toxin produced by bacteria], [a white blood cell])

#mcq(28, [A colony of bacteria growing on an agar plate is best described as], [a single bacterium], [millions of identical cells descended from one cell], [a mixture of many species], [a fungus])

#mcq(29, [Drug abuse means], [taking a prescribed medicine correctly], [taking a drug with food], [using a drug for pleasure or without medical need], [taking a drug in hospital])

#mcq(30, [A line transect is most useful for showing], [how the distribution of species changes along a line], [the total number of species], [the age of the plants], [the temperature of the soil])

#mcq(31, [The nervous system is made up of], [the brain and the spinal cord only], [the endocrine glands], [the sense organs only], [the brain, the spinal cord and the nerves])

#mcq(32, [The sense organs are best described as], [effectors], [groups of receptors that detect a particular stimulus], [parts of the brain], [glands])

#mcq(33, [A tropism is], [a directional growth response to a stimulus], [a disease of plants], [a hormone], [a type of root])

#mcq(34, [The seed coat of a seed develops from the], [ovary wall], [endosperm], [integuments of the ovule], [style])

#mcq(35, [During pregnancy the level of progesterone remains high because], [it causes ovulation], [it stimulates menstruation], [it stops the growth of the foetus], [it maintains the thickened lining of the uterus])

#mcq(36, [A seedling grown in the dark is tall but pale and weak. This is because], [it has made more food than a light-grown seedling], [cell elongation occurs without the strengthening of the cell walls], [it has more chlorophyll], [it has more roots])

#mcq(37, [A person who has been vaccinated against a disease may still catch it if], [he eats too much], [he is too old], [he drinks water], [the vaccine was stored badly and lost its potency])

#mcq(38, [Which of these is not a use of micro-organisms?], [Making yoghurt], [Producing table salt], [Producing biogas], [Making penicillin])

#mcq(39, [A pit latrine should be sited], [away from and downhill of any water source], [close to the well], [inside the kitchen], [next to the stream])

#mcq(40, [Random sampling is important because it], [makes the work easier], [reduces the number of samples needed], [avoids bias in the choice of sampling positions], [gives exact answers])

